From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 20:47:20 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 29/30] gpu_display: iceland gvm: keyboard grab
 (keyboard-shortcuts-inhibit) with CROSVM_GVM_KBD_GRAB=1

The VM window asks the compositor (KWin, Mutter) to pass its own shortcuts - Super, Alt+Tab, ... - to the VM while
the window has the keyboard focus (zwp_keyboard_shortcuts_inhibit_manager_v1). Off unless CROSVM_GVM_KBD_GRAB=1;
GVM-KBD-GRAB requested / active / inactive / unavailable on stderr for the kit rows. The protocol XML
(wayland-protocols, MIT) is bundled as the fallback the build script looks for.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
(cherry picked from commit b47d6436080e690a4638ae9287aa1f6d0517b85e)
---
 gpu_display/build.rs                          |   1 +
 ...keyboard-shortcuts-inhibit-unstable-v1.xml | 143 ++++++++++++++++++
 gpu_display/src/display_wl.c                  |  48 ++++++
 3 files changed, 192 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 gpu_display/protocol/keyboard-shortcuts-inhibit-unstable-v1.xml

diff --git a/gpu_display/build.rs b/gpu_display/build.rs
